          "sentences": [
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p02_s01",
              "sentence_ordinal": 1,
              "text": "September, 1862",
              "word_offset_start": 2,
              "word_offset_end": 4,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "paragraph_id": "doc_030_s01_p03",
          "paragraph_ordinal": 3,
          "sentences": [
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s01",
              "sentence_ordinal": 1,
              "text": "The will of God prevails.",
              "word_offset_start": 4,
              "word_offset_end": 9,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s02",
              "sentence_ordinal": 2,
              "text": "In great contests each party claims to act in accordance with the will of God.",
              "word_offset_start": 9,
              "word_offset_end": 24,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s03",
              "sentence_ordinal": 3,
              "text": "Both may be, and one must be, wrong.",
              "word_offset_start": 24,
              "word_offset_end": 32,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s04",
              "sentence_ordinal": 4,
              "text": "God cannot be for and against the same thing at the same time.",
              "word_offset_start": 32,
              "word_offset_end": 45,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s05",
              "sentence_ordinal": 5,
              "text": "In the present civil war it is quite possible that God's purpose is something different from the purpose of either party -- and yet the human instrumentalities, working just as they do, are of the best adaptation to effect His purpose.",
              "word_offset_start": 45,
              "word_offset_end": 86,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s06",
              "sentence_ordinal": 6,
              "text": "I am almost ready to say that this is probably true -- that God wills this contest, and wills that it shall not end yet.",
              "word_offset_start": 86,
              "word_offset_end": 111,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s07",
              "sentence_ordinal": 7,
              "text": "By his mere great power, on the minds of the now contestants, He could have either saved or destroyed the Union without a human contest.",
              "word_offset_start": 111,
              "word_offset_end": 136,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s08",
              "sentence_ordinal": 8,
              "text": "Yet the contest began.",
              "word_offset_start": 136,
              "word_offset_end": 140,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s09",
              "sentence_ordinal": 9,
              "text": "And, having begun He could give the final victory to either side any day.",
              "word_offset_start": 140,
              "word_offset_end": 154,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            },
            {
              "sentence_id": "doc_030_s01_p03_s10",
              "sentence_ordinal": 10,
              "text": "Yet the contest proceeds.",
              "word_offset_start": 154,
              "word_offset_end": 158,
              "authorship_note": null,
              "metaphor_instances": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
